// The write policy the test suite runs under.
//
// A real file rather than a policy built in code, because the loading path is where a policy will
// actually be got wrong: a section name capitalised differently, a pattern that matches the group
// but not the software itself. Tests that construct their own policy object never exercise it.
//
// It names exactly the fixture in assets/TestProject1.zap20 and the instances the simulation tests
// create. Anything else is refused, which is what the suite asserts in Test16GuardedWrites.
{
  "study": {
    "allow": [
      "PLC_0",
      "PLC_0/*",
      "Group1/PLC_1",
      "Group1/PLC_1/*",
      "simulation/*",
      "project"
    ],
    "deny": []
  }
}
